{"name":"Little Theatre","hex":"#73778f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"little","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Small, not large, limited, particularly:","Small, limited in size."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Not much.","Not at all."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/little"},{"term":"theatre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of theater.","A cinema; movie theatre."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/theatre"}],"entries":[{"title":"University of Adelaide","blocks":[{"text":"The University of Adelaide (UofA) was a public research university based in Adelaide, South Australia. Established in 1874, it was the third-oldest university in Australia. Its main campus in the Adelaide city centre included many sandstone buildings of historical and architectural significance, such as Bonython Hall. Its royal charter awarded by Queen Victoria in 1881 allowed it to become the second university in the English-speaking world to confer degrees to women. On 5 January 2026, it merged with the neighbouring University of South Australia to form Adelaide University. The antecedent institutions were formally disestablished after 31 March 2026, when both the University of Adelaide Act 1971 and University of South Australia Act 1990 were repealed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/51/University-of-Adelaide-Crest.svg/330px-University-of-Adelaide-Crest.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Adelaide"},{"title":"Royal Standard Theatre","blocks":[{"text":"The Royal Standard Theatre, often referred to as the Standard Theatre was a small playhouse in Sydney, Australia, situated at 223 Castlereagh Street, near the Bathurst Street corner between Bathurst and Liverpool streets, and next to the fire station. \nIt was later known as the Little Theatre and The Playhouse, and was demolished in the early 1920s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Carved_facade_of_Royal_Standard_Theatre.jpg/330px-Carved_facade_of_Royal_Standard_Theatre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Standard_Theatre"},{"title":"Little Theatre (Rochester, New York)","blocks":[{"text":"The Little Theatre, commonly known as The Little, is a movie theatre located on East Avenue in downtown Rochester, New York, and a non-profit multiplex specializing in art film, including independent and foreign productions outside the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/LittleTheatreRochesterNewYork.JPG/330px-LittleTheatreRochesterNewYork.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Theatre_(Rochester%2C_New_York)"},{"title":"Little Theatre Movement","blocks":[{"text":"As the new medium of cinema was beginning to replace theater as a source of large-scale spectacle, the Little Theatre Movement developed in the United States around 1912. The Little Theatre Movement served to provide experimental centers for the dramatic arts, free from the standard production mechanisms used in prominent commercial theaters. In several large cities, beginning with Chicago, Boston, Seattle, and Detroit, companies formed to produce more intimate, non-commercial, non-profit-centered, and reform-minded entertainments."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Theatre_Movement"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg/500px-The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg/1280px-The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg/500px-The_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_%281875%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The founders of the University of Adelaide (1875 engraving)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Founders_Of_The_Adelaide_University_by_Samuel_Calvert_-_Illustrated_Australian_News_(1875).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Heinrich_von_Angeli_%281840-1925%29_-_Queen_Victoria_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_405021_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-Heinrich_von_Angeli_%281840-1925%29_-_Queen_Victoria_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_405021_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Heinrich_von_Angeli_%281840-1925%29_-_Queen_Victoria_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_405021_-_Royal_Collection.jpg/500px-Heinrich_von_Angeli_%281840-1925%29_-_Queen_Victoria_%281819-1901%29_-_RCIN_405021_-_Royal_Collection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The royal charter grant by Queen Victoria allowed women to study at the university","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeinrich_von_Angeli_(1840-1925)_-_Queen_Victoria_(1819-1901)_-_RCIN_405021_-_Royal_Collection.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Nuclear_Fuel_Cycle_Royal_Commission_Public_Forum%2C_Bonython_Hall%2C_University_of_Adelaide%2C_22_May_2015.jpg/500px